WEBVTT

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:03.380
We had to find the Last Destiny Stone before Blackwork Raymon,

00:00:03.380 --> 00:00:06.640
but troops travel better on a full stomach, so we went for Chinese food.

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:09.320
Would you believe the restaurant belonged to Digitamamon?

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:11.960
And having the house special were Arukenimon and Mumimon.

00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:15.280
For some reason, we couldn't Digivolve, but neither could they, and they split.

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:19.620
Those two noodle brains were still hungry, so they drank from Digitamamon's secret soup pool.

00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:23.100
And inside wasn't a wonton, but the Last Destiny Stone.

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:25.310
Cody and I were finally able to DNA Digivolve.

00:00:25.310 --> 00:00:29.280
Just in time, too, 'cause Shakuromon is our last chance against Blackwork Raymon.

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:31.090
that's all you've got

00:01:31.090 --> 00:01:32.560
YEAH!

00:01:35.950 --> 00:01:36.450
KILAMA!

00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:43.340
JAMA!

00:01:43.340 --> 00:01:46.310
I'm all too

00:01:46.310 --> 00:01:53.200
KUOMA!

00:01:53.200 --> 00:02:00.000
Travel plans because his kachina bombs were sending us out!

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:01.990
We did it!

00:02:01.990 --> 00:02:07.750
You don't have to make Paildramon and Sylphimon do all the hard work!

00:02:07.750 --> 00:02:08.930
You said it.

00:02:08.930 --> 00:02:11.520
Let him have it, Jakulmon!

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:13.510
I'll prove my mettle!

00:02:13.510 --> 00:02:17.570
You're standing between me and the last Destiny Stone.

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:19.270
Now get out of my way!

00:02:19.270 --> 00:02:21.260
Who's gonna make us?

00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:22.360
Move or else?

00:02:22.360 --> 00:02:23.780
We choose Elf!

00:02:23.780 --> 00:02:26.100
Very well.

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:28.070
TERRA DESTROYER!

00:02:52.460 --> 00:02:56.410
I swallowed up Black War Greymon's Terra Force!

00:02:56.410 --> 00:02:58.640
Harmonious Spirit!

00:03:04.060 --> 00:03:07.060
Right! No matter what, protect the Destiny Stone!

00:03:07.060 --> 00:03:09.850
ME FIRST! STATIC FORM!

00:03:09.850 --> 00:03:14.110
You asked for it!

00:03:20.680 --> 00:03:27.310
Why do you persist this way? You can't win!

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:33.570
China Bob!

00:03:33.570 --> 00:03:38.440
Why do you keep trying to protect the Destiny Stones?

00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:41.520
It's a little something we call "saving the world!"

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:43.920
Desperado Blaster!

00:03:43.920 --> 00:03:48.860
How can you be so certain that what you fight for is right?

00:03:48.860 --> 00:03:50.090
Got it!

00:03:50.090 --> 00:03:53.830
Mark!

00:03:53.830 --> 00:03:55.050
Think we did it!

00:03:55.050 --> 00:03:55.750
You're right!

00:03:55.750 --> 00:03:57.650
I feel tired of this fight.

00:03:57.650 --> 00:03:59.280
I'm going to find my answer.

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:00.000
Right here.

00:04:00.280 --> 00:04:09.830
Right now, I keep asking questions of my enemies and yet I still get no answers.

00:04:09.830 --> 00:04:13.030
Why am I so different from them? Why was I created like this?

00:04:13.030 --> 00:04:16.530
Well, if they won't answer me, then why should I be concerned about them anymore?

00:04:16.530 --> 00:04:21.230
I have given every opponent the chance to convince me otherwise, but now I am through talking.

00:04:21.230 --> 00:04:25.990
Why should I care if they are destroyed, or for that matter their whole precious digital world?

00:04:25.990 --> 00:04:30.000
He seems so sad. What he needs is a friend.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:32.800
Destroying the Destiny Stone means my own destruction as well.

00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:35.920
But if that's what it takes to finally find my answer, then so be it.

00:04:37.390 --> 00:04:39.490
Take another step or else!

00:04:39.940 --> 00:04:41.520
I choose or else.

00:04:44.340 --> 00:04:48.090
It's no use, we can't stop him!

00:04:48.110 --> 00:04:51.530
But if the Destiny Stone is destroyed, the whole digital world will be lost.

00:04:51.710 --> 00:04:55.670
I'm afraid it won't only be the Digi-World, but our world will be destroyed too.

00:04:56.130 --> 00:04:57.350
Time for Plan B!

00:04:57.900 --> 00:05:00.000
By the way, does anybody know what Plan B is?

00:05:01.080 --> 00:05:02.480
We can try moving the stone!

00:05:02.480 --> 00:05:07.120
Good idea! Let's do it while the DNA Digiball Digimon are still able to hold off Blackboard Greymon!

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:10.760
How can we lift that stone? We'll never know unless we try!

00:05:10.760 --> 00:05:12.970
It's better than doing nothing!

00:05:12.970 --> 00:05:16.010
Davis is right! Besides, no one has any better ideas!

00:05:16.010 --> 00:05:17.840
I have a better idea!

00:05:17.840 --> 00:05:19.570
Say goodbye!

00:05:19.570 --> 00:05:22.470
That's your cue to cry and beg for mercy.

00:05:22.470 --> 00:05:26.420
Ready to give up.

00:05:26.420 --> 00:05:30.000
If you're ready to shut up, forget her, Davis! She's not worth it!

00:05:30.380 --> 00:05:35.380
You're trying to get me upset, but it won't work, mummy-mon.

00:05:38.200 --> 00:05:41.200
I'm going to put these kids under wraps for the last time.

00:05:44.200 --> 00:05:45.200
Nightmare Syndrome!

00:05:46.200 --> 00:05:51.780
I warned you not to drink out of the Chinese soup spring.

00:05:51.780 --> 00:05:53.780
You'll pay for that.

00:05:54.770 --> 00:05:56.610
Take care of the Destiny Stone, kids!

00:05:56.610 --> 00:05:57.560
Don't worry!

00:05:57.560 --> 00:05:59.390
Thanks, Digi-Tam-a-mon. Thanks, Tape-a-mon.

00:05:59.390 --> 00:06:00.000
Thanks, Tape-a-mon.

00:06:00.480 --> 00:06:03.170
Now's our chance, let's go.

00:06:03.170 --> 00:06:06.080
How do we move that thing?

00:06:06.080 --> 00:06:09.420
I got it!

00:06:09.420 --> 00:06:11.770
Let's try using the old D3s.

00:06:11.770 --> 00:06:13.620
Mm-hm-hm.

00:06:13.620 --> 00:06:26.840
Mm-hm-hm.

00:06:26.840 --> 00:06:27.770
Doing it.

00:06:27.770 --> 00:06:28.930
Binding into one.

00:06:31.690 --> 00:06:33.650
This is what I need, another flashlight.

00:06:33.650 --> 00:06:36.490
What are those kids doing back there with the Destiny Stone?

00:06:36.490 --> 00:06:38.320
I just hope they don't eat all the soup.

00:07:22.360 --> 00:07:26.490
I saw when Blackboard Raymon he stones. He's huge!

00:07:26.490 --> 00:07:29.350
That guy's almost as big as my appetite!

00:07:31.150 --> 00:07:34.150
They don't know how to fight, 'cause Blackbird Greymon's been looking for him.

00:07:34.150 --> 00:07:39.300
Finally, my ultimate opponent has appeared.

00:07:39.300 --> 00:07:42.460
You.

00:07:42.460 --> 00:07:45.800
You are the one with the accursed soul of darkness.

00:07:45.800 --> 00:07:48.670
Soul of darkness?

00:07:48.670 --> 00:07:50.550
You can't mean me.

00:07:50.550 --> 00:07:54.420
Tell me, why do you destroy the Destiny Stones?

00:07:54.420 --> 00:07:57.890
I did it to make you appear so we can fight.

00:07:57.890 --> 00:07:59.950
You are stronger than me.

00:08:00.380 --> 00:08:07.780
Digimon I've ever seen before do you have any idea who I am only that you are

00:08:07.780 --> 00:08:15.140
my ultimate opponent I am a Zoolong Mom a Zoolong I am the guardian of the Eastern

00:08:15.140 --> 00:08:18.420
Hemisphere of the digital world and the keeper of the spheres of light and hope

00:08:18.420 --> 00:08:22.480
because you have destroyed the destiny stones this world has become unbalanced

00:08:22.480 --> 00:08:26.960
do you understand the consequences of what you have done I don't care about

00:08:26.960 --> 00:08:30.000
any of that nonsense fight me a Zoolong Mon

